c2  try to sort of work through this cognitive dissonance where Trump calls everything a hoax, and, you know, she`s on news back saying, well, it`s not a hoax, like he abused 14-year-old girls. That`s not a hoax.\par \par \uc2 And watching someone who believes Trump`s claims of hoax Ness in 99 percent of the time, but get to the one percent and have to wrestle with the fact that, like, oh, maybe he just lies about what`s a hoax.\par \par \uc2 WELCH: I think we`ve all underestimated \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  a bit. I think she is actually playing a long game here. Moses Mike is playing the short game. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  requires a lot of coddling, and so all of these MAGA men are full-blown coddling Trump at all time in his ego.\par \par \uc2 Marjorie, Taylor Greene is talking about Israel, Gaza. She is messaging to the MAGA base. Are we really America first, or are we Israel first? She`s standing up for the Epstein thing. I think she has bigger political ambitions. We`re seeing that play out. She hangs out with \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  all the time, who I think is a nut, but he is a political strategist.\par \par \uc2 And I think we`re starting to see these fissures in the MAGA base, because some people are not playing the short-sighted game anymore. Trump`s quacking like a duck. His ankles are swollen as all get out. Clearly, has dementia. And I think some of the more ambitious MAGA people are starting to break away and feed information to the base, because they`re seeing what their careers can be post-MAGA. And I think \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  is doing that.\par \par \uc2 GOLDBERG: Well, you know what I thought was fantastically telling. I mean, I don`t know how much you`ve talked about this James O`Keefe bust on this show.\par \par \uc2 HAYES: We haven`t, because he`s such an untrustworthy figure.\par \par \uc2 GOLDBERG: Such an untrustworthy figure. And he basically, he sent, you know, kind of a cat fisher. He sent some to basically get somebody