\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 CHRIS JANSING REPORTS for March 24, 2023, MSNBC\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Jansing, Tim Miller, Vaughn Hillyard, Ken Dilanian, Joyce  Vance, Kelly O`Donnell, Jake Sherman, Tom Costello, David Ignatius \par \uc2 7,700 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 March 2023\par \uc2 MSNBC: Meet the Press Daily\par \uc2 MSNMPD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 CQ-Roll Call, Inc. All rights reserved. Prepared by CQ-Roll Call, Inc. \par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [13:00:26]\par \par \uc2 CHRIS JANSING, MSNBC HOST: Good day. I`m Chris Jansing. Live at MSNBC headquarters in New York City.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump`s attorney now calling for an investigation into the investigators. The latest attempt to smear Manhattan D.A. \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  and derail the hush money probe. It comes after Trump himself posted three dozen times in the past day and a half, repeatedly attacking Bragg calling him human scum and a danger to the country. The former president with no shortage of things to say, but are his supporters still listening.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the bigger legal danger for Trump may not be in New York but in D.C. What Trump`s own attorney might have told the grand jury today about documents that Trump had stashed at Mar-a-Lago. And the U.S. sends F-15s to bomb Iranian-backed groups in eastern Syria after a deadly attack on Americans ever local military base. One of two attacks in the past 36 hours. A live update from the Pentagon is just an hour away.\par \par \uc2 And take a look at this video. That`s Manuel Oliver, the father of one of the teenagers killed in the Parkland massacre, handcuffed on the floor of the Capitol. We`ll tell you why and talk to him coming up.\par \par \uc2 But we start with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  squeezed in the vise of multiple criminal investigations and lashing out at his adversaries in a series of increasingly frantic online posts over the past 36 hours. Now the majority had been aimed at the Manhattan D.A. \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , calling him everything from a degenerate psychopath to an animal doing the devil`s work and warning that an indictment could lead to death and destruction across America.\par \par \uc2 He even retweeted this article showing him with a bat next to another photo of Bragg`s head. But all of this is also serving as a rallying cry to his base and a plea for donations ahead of Trump`s first major campaign rally tomorrow night in Waco, Texas.\par \par \uc2 I want to bring in NBC`s Vaughn Hillyard live outside Mar-a-Lago in West Palm Beach. Tim Miller is writer-at-large for The Bulwark and an MSNBC political analyst. Tim, what is all this? Is Trump just venting? Is he money raising? Is he just whipping up the base? Is the pressure getting to him? What do you think`s going on here?\par \par \uc2 TIM MILLER, MSNBC POLITICAL ANALYST: Yes. Well, I hope Vaughn staying safe down there. Yes, I think that he is venting. But this is a deranged person. I think it`s important to step back, we can look at the politics but also just the reality for a second. If you were reading these bleats that he`s been sending out for the past 24 hours out loud, and a coffee shop, people would be running away from you. And I`m calling for the manager.\par \par \uc2 I mean, these are the utterings of an insane person, not somebody that has the mental capacity to be president in 2024. I think it`s important to say that clearly. I think it`s a reflection of the fact that he is both angered and upset about the possibility of these impending indictments, but also sees the political benefit. This is a cunning guy, he might be a little deranged, but he`s definitely cunning and has this animal ability to know what is going to get his base riled up.\par \par \uc2 And you can see it in the data already, that the MAGA voters are wanting to stand by their man over this. And \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  thinks that he can use that and these threats of violence, these threats of political action to his benefit.\par \par \uc2 JANSING: So, Vaughn, as we talk about all the different ways that he has been venting if that`s what`s happening here. I also mentioned this new letter from Trump`s attorney which was posted by the former president about 90 minutes ago. Tell us about it. And maybe what it does say about the President`s -- former President`s state of mind right now.\par \par \uc2 VAUGHN HILLYARD, NBC NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Right. His legal counsel, not only in Manhattan, but we saw a similar type of a letter and appeal to judge down in Fulton County, Georgia, trying to make the case legally that the investigations into them are prosecutorial misconduct. This letter from Joe Tacopina, his is lawyer in Manhattan outlines to the New York City Department of investigations over the course of multiple pages, reasoning that they claim that \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  is conducting this for political calculations.\par \par \uc2 For \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , this is an effort to essentially say to Republicans, are you with me or you against me? As Tim just outlined here, we have seen time and again, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  put pressure on those within the Republican Party to have his back and that is why when he goes to South Carolina on a campaign stop, it`s notable when you see the likes of \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  and Governor McMaster standing by his side.\par \par \uc2 [13:05:05]\par \par \uc2 When he goes to Iowa, he has Governor \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2  standing by his side. That pressure is only going to continue to mount. And when you look at polling over the course of the last several years from the impeachments, to January 6, that Republican base of support really does not move away from him. In a general election, it`s a whole different conversation. But we`re talking about a republican nomination process.\par \par \uc2 And what you see over the course of these last -- especially 12 hours in which he is suggesting that there could be, "potential death and destruction if he were charged." He`s warning his supporters that there could be "turmoil, hatred and chaos for years to come," if he is charged, he is suggesting that this is anarchy and the work of the devil. He is sending out flyers to his supporters, American voters around the country, that now is the time to come to his defense.\par \par \uc2 And if he were to go sit before the criminal proceedings before a jury, ultimately, they`d have to say whether he was guilty or innocent, but it`s going to be the voters who will have to say whether he is going to be the Republican nominee and ultimately the president come 2025.\par \par \uc2 JANSING: And we talk all the time about the voters who are his base, Tim. And one measure of that has been that they have supported him financially in extraordinary ways. However, in the three days after he said he was going to be arrested this past Tuesday, he raised about a million and a half dollars. Compare that to a million dollars a day after the raid on Mar-a-Lago. Do you think there`s worth extrapolating anything out of that? Do his posts have the same impact they once had?\par \par \uc2 MILLER: Well, a million and a half dollars is nothing. I mean, I think that he knows that this is squeezing money and his team knows that they`re squeezing money out of folks. I don`t know if it was an intentional plan to leak the, you know, arrests on Tuesday on his fake \uc2 Twitter\uc2  because it can help them raise money, but they definitely acted like it was an intentional plan. He began sending out these missives, you know, these fundraising missives immediately after that.\par \par \uc2 I was amused to see some of the \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  supporters, you know, out there, trying to tell people hey, this guy is grifting, this guy`s stealing, this guy`s conning you. It`s like, well, no kidding. It`s what he`s been doing for eight years. He`s good at this. He knows how to get money out of his supporters. He knows -- he knows how to get money out of supporters, both in politics and in the private sector.\par \par \uc2 He`s done this with all of his different branding endeavors that Trump stakes all the way down. And so, I think he sees this as a financial opportunity for sure. Now, is the money quite as much as when the raid came? No, but I don`t think we can take a lot from that until we see if he actually is indicted. You know, what the financial responses then.\par \par \uc2 JANSING: Well, you bring up \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . So, let`s talk about him, Tim. He had a maybe a little rougher time recently rolling out his ideas on national and international issues. One Republican told Politico it was, "a momentum speed bump for DeSantis." Partly, because Trump has dominated the news cycle, but also because of what are perceived as missteps on things like Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 So last night, he actually denied that he had amended his position after he was criticized for calling the war a territorial dispute. Listen.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GOV. RON DESANTIS (R-FL): I care more about securing our own border in the United States than I do about the Russia Ukraine border. And it seems like the establishment, some of the people that you mentioned, they ignore the problems that we have here at home as Americans.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JANSING: So, what do you make of this? I mean, first of all, is going on with friendly journalists like Piers Morgan and \uc2 Newsmax\uc2  going to help get him ready for the national stage if indeed he does announce, but do you think he`s had a little bit of a momentum blip here?\par \par \uc2 MILLER: Yes. He`s going to stay in the media, the conservative media mobile, that`s for sure. You know what this is reminiscent of, Chris, is back in 2016. What happened when Scott Walker came out of the gate, remember all this, you know, people might not remember but in like May of 2015, Scott Walker was the hot ticket, because a lot 