o they resist taking Ethan home, they don`t let school authorities know that he had access to a firearm. And so, it`s unusual to see parents charged. I think this case may just be a one off. But given the fact here that the panel has now ruled that there`s a meritorious legal theory and a jury can consider the evidence and decide whether or not the parents should be convicted.\par \par \uc2 JANSING: Assuming it does go to trial, Joyce, and we know that we are a country that is deeply divided on the use the ownership of guns. How much of his case might be won or lost in jury selection?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Well, I think all cases are won or lost in jury selection to some extent. But what the judge will ask the jury to do in this case is to set aside any views they may have on gun laws. And really, this is not a case that turns on your Second Amendment views, because even people who are strongly in support of Second Amendment rights, still believe that guns at least I hope, still believe that guns shouldn`t be used for school shootings, will be persuaded that these parents did not do an appropriate job of securing their firearms or training their child.\par \par \uc2 Something that people with strong second American views -- strong second amendment views often advocate for. And so, the court and prosecutors will have to be careful about ensuring that jurors consider only the evidence in the case and don`t let anything extraneous creep in. But I don`t think it`ll be different in that regard for many other cases involving gun violence.\par \par \uc2 JANSING: Joyce Vance, always great to have you on the program. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 House Republicans heading to jail in D.C. What they`re doing there and why a couple of Democrats are tagging along? We have that next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [13:30:41]\par \par \uc2 JANSING: Relitigating the insurrection. Right now \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  is leading a group of House Republicans visiting January 6th defendants in jail. Axios reports two progressive Democrats are joining the group in order to, quote, "cut through Republicans` attempts to whitewash the dangerous realities of January 6th."\par \par \uc2 Twenty people charged in connection with the riot at being held in the D.C. jail. Nine of them have been convicted or pled guilty. Among those currently in the jail Daniel Rodriguez who pled guilty to driving a stun gun into the neck of former D.C. police officer \uc2 Michael Fanone\uc2  and Samuel Lazar accused of using a bullhorn to urge rioters to steal police officers` guns.\par \par \uc2 I want to bring in Jake Sherman, co-founder of "Punchbowl News" and an MSNBC political contributor. Tim Miller is back with us.\par \par \uc2 So, Jake, \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  claims and she wrote a big letter that she posted on her Web site that she`s received reports of abuse in the jail and of conditions that -- these are her words -- paint a picture of despair, hopelessness, and the severe abuse of justice. So is her goal here jail reform?\par \par \uc2 JAKE SHERMAN, PUNCHBOWL NEWS CO-FOUNDER: I don`t know what her goal is, Chris? One of the craziest things I`ve seen in this majority is Republicans` desire to keep January 6th which I was -- I lived through. I was there, I know what happened quite well, to keep it in the news. I don`t understand that. Kevin McCarthy handed over 42,000 or so hours of video footage to \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 . I don`t quite understand that either.\par \par \uc2 January 6th according to people who are sane and who understand what happened on that day was an atrocious day in which people tried to, as we see in these images, storm the Capitol to try to stop the count of the 2020 election because they thought for some reason it was fraudulent. It`s no more difficult than that and Republicans` desire to keep it in the news quite frankly is -- I don`t quite understand it.\par \par \uc2 JANSING: Yes, and Tim, we mentioned the two