 skiff and seeing what we can find out from briefings.\par \par \uc2 The Senate Intelligence and House Intelligence Committee holds frequent briefings on intelligence matters. So, I think you`re going to see that right away. You`re going to see, you know, intelligence officials, probably from the CIA, the NSC on Capitol Hill briefing members of Congress. And we just -- we don`t know what which way this will turn, proverbially and literally, both politically and where this balloon will go.\par \par \uc2 But I think the important point to note is, there is some difference between what Republicans and Democrats are saying. Republicans are saying they should shoot this thing out of the sky. Democrats have not gone that far yet, for the most part.\par \par \uc2 JANSING: Jake Sherman, Courtney Kube, thank you both. I know we`ll be seeing more of you through the day. Now to that epic once in a lifetime cold snap. It`s gripping New England right now. Windshields forecast to drop so low. Numbers, frankly, are looking like a mistake. Look at this forecast from our NBC affiliate in northern Maine where it could get close to 60 below, which can cause frostbite in less than two minutes. And Maine isn`t alone. Millions are suffering.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Lots and lots of layers, those handwarmers coming in clutch this morning. It is brutally cold out here.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Doctors are saying to people that they should just not underestimate just how dangerously cold -- this cold snap will be.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: These will be some of the coldest feeling temperatures that a lot of us have experienced in our lifetimes.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JANSING: In fact, we could see all-time records broken in some places but nowhere is colder than Mount Washington, New Hampshire where it could bottom out -- are you ready for this? At minus 100.\par \par \uc2 [13:10:10]\par \par \uc2 Right now, 