s achievements, but he got it right. And the threat to democracy is important.\par \par \uc2 Moving forward, though, I think it`s critically important that Biden and the Senate Democrats come up with a strong agenda that the Republicans are going to look foolish for rejecting. And especially when it comes to legislation on electoral reform. That could be very important to Biden moving forward. But he should also use the first six months of this year to take more of a victory lap for the tremendous two years he had his first -- you know, during his first term in office.\par \par \uc2 WITT: Philip, when do you think we`re going to hear from Biden on his 2024 plans? How quickly?\par \par \uc2 RUCKER: You know, it`s true that he was planning to discuss this with his family over the holidays, which he`s doing that this week down in St. Croix. Now I don`t know if we`re going to hear any sort of public announcement about his intentions in January but we could start to hear some rumblings from his camp. Some preparations they might be making towards a bid. But I would not anticipate a formal announcement until a little bit later closer to the spring. He`s in no need to lock this up right away. He`s got a little bit of time here to figure it out.\par \par \uc2 WITT: OK. On the flip side, Susan, what are you hearing from Republican candidates who are trying to figure out their own decisions on whether to challenge \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ? Do you think those announcements could come fairly soon?\par \par \uc2 DEL PERCIO: My guess is closer to the spring, maybe March, April, because they do want to see what happens with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 [13:35:01]\par \par \uc2 I mean, Phil`s next book could be "Trump Alone Broke It" and he could be talking about his campaign because his campaign is truly unraveling. But seriously, it`s just -- we just don`t know where things are going with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . There are several lawsuits that are coming up that are going 