\par \par \uc2 JANSING: We have had a lot to talk about, Kristen, Tom, Carol, Charlie, \uc2 Carol Lam\uc2 , Vaughn, thanks to all of you.\par \par \uc2 President Biden, any other day this would have been an hour addressing world leaders at the \uc2 U.N\uc2 . just hours after \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  issues new threats. We`re going to talk about that on CHRIS JANSING REPORTS, next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [13:50:51]\par \par \uc2 JANSING: Some very high stakes diplomacy on display this morning, as President Biden took the United Nations stage to address world leaders and new threats from \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Just today, President Putin has made overt nuclear threats against Europe in a reckless disregard for the responsibilities of a nonproliferation regime. Now Russia is calling, calling out more soldiers to join the fight, and the Kremlin is organizing a sham referendum to try to annex parts of Ukraine, an extremely significant violation of the \uc2 U.N\uc2 . charter.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JANSING: That was in response to the Russian leader`s national address overnight to announce a large scale military mobilization of his war in Ukraine following a series of stunning battlefield setbacks over the last month.\par \par \uc2 For more, let`s bring in Barry McCaffrey, a retired four-star general who served as a division commander in the Gulf War. He is an NBC News and MSNBC military analyst.\par \par \uc2 Putin didn`t just say he was mobilizing more troops. He said he was going to use everything at his disposal, basically. What`s he doing here?\par \par \uc2 BARRY MCCAFFREY, MSNBC MILITARY ANALYST: I think Putin in increasingly desperate circumstances, politically, economically, militarily, the announcement by way of one secret clause, I would note that it was pre- recorded, not a live presentation. But essentially, he thinks