oday telling the \uc2 U.N\uc2 . that there was a Russian strike on the railway station in the Dnipro region that injured 50 people. Unclear how many people if any might have died in that attack.\par \par \uc2 Here in Kyiv we`ve also heard the air raid sirens go off more than half a dozen times today and the day is not over. In the past, many of the strikes that had been particularly damaging have taken place after nightfall so people are not letting their guard down quite yet. But in the meantime, there`s been a real vibe of pride and defiance here in the capital and in other places in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Today we saw \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 , the prime minister of U.K. here, making an announcement about more than 50 million pounds of aid. Obviously the president of the United States announced that the $3 billion package you mentioned which includes new surface-to-air missiles for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 And in the streets of Kyiv today we saw lots of people out and about in traditional clothing, some of them having draped themselves in the blue and yellow of the Ukrainian flag, trying to signify that they are, you know, still here, standing strong six months after a war started that President Putin anticipated was going to be over very shortly. Yasmin?\par \par \uc2 VOSSOUGHIAN: A country surviving amidst this utter destruction that they`ve had to experience over the last six months.\par \par \uc2 Josh, I know you`ve got to go. So thank you for your reporting on that.\par \par \uc2 Lieutenant General, let`s dig into some of this and some of the reporting that we heard from Josh there and talk specifically about where Russia is right now. Early on in this war you actually predicted that Russia would fail to take Kyiv. That, in fact, is true. It seems as if they have now kind of stationed themselves in the eastern part of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Do you believe that is where they will remain or they will continue to make gains west in Ukraine or try to, at least?\par 