ned to do what he must do before we wind up in a bloody fight. We all know that the fight is coming.\par \par \uc2 CHILDRESS: The Oath Keepers began planning to block the peaceful transfer of power shortly after the November 3 election and according to the Department of Justice, Stewart Rhodes, the Oath Keepers` leader, said to his followers that we were not going to get through this without a civil war.\par \par \uc2 In response to the December 19, 2020 tweet by President Trump, the Oath Keepers focused on January 6 in Washington DC. In response to the tweet, one member, the president of the Florida chapter, put it on social media. The president called us to the Capitol. He wants us to make it wild. The goal was for the Oath keepers to be called to duty so that they could keep the president in power although President Trump had just lost the election.\par \par \uc2 The committee learned that the Oath Keepers set up quick reaction forces outside of the city in Virginia where they stored arms. The goal of these quick reaction forces was to be on standby just in case President Trump invoked the Insurrection Act.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Do the Oath Keepers ever provide weapons to members?\par \par \uc2 RHODES: I`m going to decline to answer that and put it from the grounds for due process grounds.\par \par \uc2 CHILDRESS: In footage obtained by the committee, we learned that on the night of January 5, \uc2 Enrique Tarrio\uc2  and Stewart Rhodes met in a parking garage in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 TARRIO: There`s a mutual respect there. I think we`re fighting the same fight and I think that`s what`s important.\par \par \uc2 CHILDRESS: The committee learned that the Oath Keepers went into the Capitol for the East doors in two stack formations. The DOJ alleges that one of the stacks went into the Capitol looking for Speaker Pelosi, although they never found her. As the attack was unfolding, Mr. Tarrio took credit.\par \par \uc2 And documents obtained by the Department of Justice, Mr. Tarrio said in an encrypted chat, make no mistake and we did this. Later on that evening, Mr. Tarrio even posted a video, which seemed to resemble him in front of the Capitol with a black cape and the title of the video was a premonition.\par \par \uc2 [13:05:00]\par \par \uc2 The evidence developed by the select committee and the Department of Justice highlights how each group participated in the attack on the Capitol on January 6. In fact, the investigation revealed that it was individuals associated with the Proud Boys who instigated the initial breach at the Peace circle at 12:33 p.m. Within 10 minutes, rioters had already filled a lower west plaza. By two o`clock, rioters had reached the doors on the west and the east plazas. And by 2:13, rioters had actually broken through the Senate wing door and got into the Capitol building.\par \par \uc2 A series of breaches followed. At 2:25 p.m., rioters breached the east side doors to the rotunda, and then right after 2:40 p.m., rioters reached the side doors near the Ways and Means room. Once the rioters infiltrated the Capitol, they moved to the crypt, the rotunda, the hallways leading to the House chambers, and even inside the Senate chambers.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 TUR: Let us bring an NBC News digital justice reporter Ryan Reilly, \uc2 Clint Watts\uc2 , a distinguished research fellow at the Foreign Policy Research Institute, and an NBC News National Security Analyst, also Jeh Johnson, former DHS Secretary under President Obama, and partner Paul, Weiss.\par \par \uc2 All right, Ryan, I want to begin with you. Last night`s hearing -- at last night`s hearing, \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  said -- after it, excuse me that the committee had evidence that the Proud Boys were in contact with Donald Trump`s orbit. And that`ll come out later in the hearings. I want to know what you think about that. And you also just got a hold of some brand new video filmed by a rioter`s \uc2 GoPro\uc2  and released by the DC district court as evidence. What does that video show?\par \par \uc2 RYAN REILLY, MSNBC JUSTICE REPORTER: Yes, that video is pretty compelling. You know, this video continues to trickle out. NBC News is part of a media coalition that is pushing for access to some of this footage. And, you know, it shows essentially, and I think the language in this is especially is really gripping because it shows that there is this push against the police pile that they were really determined to get inside. They didn`t care who was standing in their way.\par \par \uc2 It is also just sort of amazing when you just think about the fact that someone filmed this on their own with their \uc2 GoPro\uc2 , right? It`s creating a record of their criminal intent, and what they were -- you know, filming themselves doing crimes. But it also speaks to this idea that they thought that they were going to win this. They thought they would be on the right side of history and that Trump would stay president and that this was going to be something to be proud of. So it`s kind of revealing I think. It`s in the mindset of the individuals who stormed the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 As far as it goes, the evidence we heard last night about this idea that the Oath Keepers were in communication with someone in Trump`s orbit, I`m really -- there was a hearing a few weeks back where the third Oath Keeper pleaded guilty to seditious conspiracy. And that`s one of the first times this revelation took place. He talked about being at the Phoenix Park Hotel, actually right near the NBC Bureau and a few blocks from the Capitol, in this suite with Stewart Rhodes, when Stewart Rhodes was calling someone, who he was trying to get in touch directly with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And this was on the evening of January 6 after the Capitol have already been breached, and was still trying to get Trump to invoke the Insurrection Act, and bring in all of these different quick-reaction forces that were outside of the Capitol, outside of DC to try to take over the government. So it really is this extraordinary moment and that`s the only thing I`m looking for next is who is that individual in Trump`s circle who was in touch with the Proud Boys?\par \par \uc2 JACKSON: Hey, Ryan, it`s Hallie. Before we let you go, you know, there`s -- you know probably every frame of the videos that have come out since January 6. And I know you`ve talked to some of these online sleuths who had been helping law enforcement identify folks who are at the -- at the insurrection. What did they think as you`re talking with these sources of yours about the video that was presented -- the new images, the new audio presented by the committee less than 24 hours ago?\par \par \uc2 REILLY: Yes, you know, ahead of the hearing, I think there was a little bit of skepticism about whether or not they would be able to turn up and do things that the sleuths have already found already, but they were impressed. I mean, they have access to all of this surveillance footage. And I think especially putting audio over that surveillance footage, which doesn`t necessarily come with audio is really compelling for that presentation because it shows a lot of these moments and how big the mob was.\par \par \uc2 JACKSON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 REILLY: And especially when you see it, from sort of a bird`s eye view at the top of the Capitol. And in the surveillance images inside the Capitol, it`s just extraordinarily compelling. So there`s a lot more evidence to come. And that`s going to be used to identify individuals in the future. The more video that comes out through the committee process and through the legal process is going to continue to be used to identify individuals and potentially bring criminal charges against them.\par \par \uc2 MITCHELL: Jeh Johnson --\par \par \uc2 JACKSON: Ryan Reilly, thank you so much for being with us. Appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 MITCHELL: Sorry. And thank you, Ryan, as well from me. I want to bring in Jeh Johnson. As a former Homeland Security Secretary, how alarming are these connections between the Oath Keepers and the Proud Boys?\par \par \uc2 [13:10:00]\par \par \uc2 The fact that there was that meeting. They were in the garage right underneath where we`re sitting now the night before that they were planning, that they were talking to each other. Both of those groups now have been charged with seditious conspiracy to overthrow the government, so very serious felony charge, at least that accusation. What do we know about the way homeland and DOJ and other agencies track these extremist groups, these domestic terrorists?\par \par \uc2 JEH JOHNSON, FORMER SECRETARY OF HOMELAND SECURITY: Andrea, DHS through its bulletins, has been increasingly sounding the alarm about these groups. I have to say, and this goes back to the discussion you were having a moment ago. I recall vividly the moment after that debate, that presidential debate ended and there was such explicit discussion of the Proud Boys in that debate, that Proud Boy membership was going to soar right after that. And it -- and it did, in fact.\par \par \uc2 Andrea, what I -- what I heard last night from that hearing, and I hear I`m -- in my role is former federal prosecutor which I was over 30 years ago. The committee is very clearly making the case for the Department of Justice of a criminal act by none other than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . The committee chair now uses the words attempted coup attempt to overthrow the government in connection with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It`s also notable that the Proud Boys have been indicted as part of a seditious conspiracy. It sounds as if the committee is making the case that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  -- \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  joined in that seditious conspiracy. There is also the charge of insurrection, acts of violence against the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2 , as well as those who give aid and comfort there, too. In my judgment