y happy with the direction.\par \par \uc2 TODD: Well and I do. I'm going to put up the negative side of this and this is to me, Xochitl, why we saw the words ultra MAGA. OK? Let me put this up. You know, after defunding the police is the least popular thing you can do, OK? That -- we've got that. But then the next four issues, Trump winning the election is a minus 35. A \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  endorsement is a minus 27. Right? Overturning Roe v. Wade minus 26.\par \par \uc2 A Trump endorsement minus 20. Then you get down to AOC and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , but it's sort of two through -- two through five there, Xochitl, cheap I see why there is this idea that, well, if you can create the -- do you want ultra MAGA policies?\par \par \uc2 [13:10:08]\par \par \uc2 I get. But that's a hard sell. It takes time.\par \par \uc2 HINOJOSA: Well, they -- you're pulling absolutely right here. That's exactly what the White House is seeing right now. They understand that if they talk about the far right and the far-right sort of taking over, if the far right takes over the ultra MAGA, takes over the House and the Senate, you will overturn Roe v. Wade. All these things will happen. We -- our elections will be at stake.\par \par \uc2 And if you put Republican Secretaries of State, they might try to overturn these elections. So what Democrats are doing and what the White House is doing right now is they're trying to raise the stakes, they're trying to tell people listen, don't stay home in the midterm elections. There is a clear choice between Democrats and Republicans right now. And if you don't go out and vote, you could end up with this ultra MAGA Congress that could impact you in your daily lives.\par \par \uc2 TODD: Well, we have -- we do have a primary coming up on Tuesday. We got Brendan here. He's Mr. Georgia. Camp winning as big as he's winning, Trump sort of throwing a temper tantrum about it. What does that mean for the general?\par \par \uc2 BUCK: Yes. So we've seen