ing is considered a win.\par \par \uc2 My responsibility is not to the gridlock and politics of Washington, it`s to the citizens of New Hampshire, and I`d rather push myself 120 miles an hour delivering wins for New Hampshire than to slow down and end up on Capitol Hill debating partisan politics without results. That`s why I`m going to run for a fourth term.\par \par \uc2 (END OF VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TODD: It`s not hard to connect Sununu`s decision not to run to former President Trump`s outsized influence in Republican politics, too. Sununu would have had a harder time getting out of the primary perhaps than he would have in the general. And while he supported Trump`s 2020 run, Sununu has pushed back against the former president`s ongoing lie that the election was stolen.\par \par \uc2 Some Republicans had hoped that Youngkin`s victory in Virginia would show Sununu that you can run for office without being a vocal Trump supporter but it looks like that didn`t happen at least in New Hampshire.\par \par \uc2 [13:45:01]\par \par \uc2 And it`s important to note, Sununu did not rule out a run for president at his press conference this morning. New Hampshire isn`t a bad place to start a campaign for the White House last time I checked. Remember Sununu`s brother served in the Senate. Sununu`s his father was a White House chief of staff. Chris Sununu knew everything about how Washington works. He had a pretty good team of advisers so it`s not like he didn`t have a lot of good information to process when he made this decision.\par \par \uc2 It`s a big blow to the GOP on this one and you can probably say it`s Donald Trump`s first win or loss depending on how you want to look at it when it comes to Republican Senate recruiting wars.\par \par \uc2 Coming up, a new development in a story we first brought to you on "MEET THE PRESS REPORTS." We`re going to head to Texas where one principal just got fired over false accusations of teaching critical race theory.\par \par \uc2 